{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q121881","formula":"Co₂O₃","hill":"Co2O3","elements":["O","Co"],"composition":{"O":3.0,"Co":2.0},"names":{"en":"Cobalt(III) oxide","ru":"Оксид кобальта(III)","uk":"Оксид кобальту(III)"},"descriptions":{"en":"Cobalt(III) oxide is the inorganic compound with the formula of Co2O3. Although only two oxides of cobalt are well characterized, CoO and Co3O4, procedures claiming to give Co2O3 have been described. The treatment of Co(II) salts such as cobalt(II) sulfate with an aqueous solution of sodium hypochlorite (also known as bleach) gives a black solid: 2CoSO4 + 4NaOH + NaOCl → Co2O3 + 2Na2SO4 + NaCl Some formulations of the catalyst hopcalite contain \"Co2O3\".","ru":"Оксид кобальта(III) — неорганическое соединение, оксид металла кобальта с формулой Co2O3, чёрные кристаллы, не растворимые в воде.","uk":"Окси́д ко́бальту(III), ко́бальт(III) окси́д — неорганічна сполука складу Co2O3. Являє собою чорні, гексагональні кристали."},"fame":24,"pubchemCid":4110762,"mass":165.865,"charge":0,"smiles":"O=[Co]O[Co]=O","inchikey":"UPWOEMHINGJHOB-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"oxo(oxocobaltiooxy)cobalt","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-1043418","atoms":69,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[3.018,0.0,0.0],[0.0,9.849,0.0],[0.0,0.0,15.216]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":3.565,"z":8.332,"el":"Co"},{"x":3.018,"y":3.565,"z":8.332,"el":"Co"},{"x":1.509,"y":1.36,"z":6.885,"el":"Co"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.565,"z":14.493,"el":"Co"},{"x":3.018,"y":3.565,"z":14.493,"el":"Co"},{"x":1.509,"y":1.36,"z":0.724,"el":"Co"},{"x":1.509,"y":4.021,"z":2.131,"el":"Co"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.903,"z":13.085,"el":"Co"},{"x":3.018,"y":0.903,"z":13.085,"el":"Co"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.903,"z":9.739,"el":"Co"},{"x":3.018,"y":0.903,"z":9.739,"el":"Co"},{"x":1.509,"y":4.021,"z":5.477,"el":"Co"},{"x":0